{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"## 🟡 §7 — What NetworkPolicy Cannot Do\n\nTwo facts. This section teaches two facts and nothing else, and the first one is the highest-consequence sentence in the chapter.\n\n### The prerequisite\n\n**"}},"session_id":"0aa5f650-2fa0-47cb-b50a-0fd37e7f3f0a","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"31dfb8c7-d0eb-40c4-8a49-f4f244d81232"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"Network policies are implemented by the network plugin. To use network policies, you must be using a networking solution which supports NetworkPolicy. Creating a NetworkPolicy resource without a controller that implements it will have"}},"session_id":"0aa5f650-2fa0-47cb-b50a-0fd37e7f3f0a","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"4df23731-771a-44cd-9559-ae66bc0de52d"}
